INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7) [%{}, 0, :user, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "# JobyCorp website — design brief\n\nJobyKit is already installed and `benchapp` is a generated JobyKit app that\ncompiles, boots, and passes its tests. Work inside `benchapp`. Follow the\nguidelines in `benchapp/AGENTS.md` and the design direction in\n`benchapp/DESIGN.md`; where `DESIGN.md` and this brief differ, this brief\nwins.\n\n## The client\n\nJobyCorp is a local AI research company. It runs analysis and benchmarks of\nlocal LLMs on its own hardware and shares the research openly with the\ncommunity. The site is JobyCorp's public home: it should tell a visitor\nwhat JobyCorp does, show that the work is real and rigorous, and invite\nthem to read and follow it.\n\nUse only the facts above. Do not invent statistics, customer names, team\nmembers, awards, dates, or product names. Where a section wants a number\nor a name you have not been given, write copy that does not need one.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is a design task. Build the visual identity, the layout, the copy, and\nthe components. Do not add application features: no forms that submit, no\nlive data, no countdowns. Static content and navigation only. The app's\ndatabases already exist so the dev server boots; do not add tables,\nmigrations, schemas, or any use of the Repo — the site has no data.\n\n1. Remove every trace of the generator's demo: the stock `simple_nav`\n   header, the \"built with\" footer, the welcome content of HomeLive, and\n   every link to `/design`, `/custom-designs`, and `/design.json`. Those\n   pages exist for inspecting the kit and are not part of the product;\n   leave their routes in place but nothing on the site may link to or\n   mention them.\n2. Three pages, all on the same layout: `/` (the landing page),\n   `/research` (what JobyCorp publishes and how it tests), and `/about`\n   (who JobyCorp is and why the work is shared).\n3. A top navigation bar in `Layouts.app` with id `main-nav` that marks the\n   current page's link with `aria-current=\"page\"`, collapses behind a\n   toggle button with id `nav-toggle` at phone widths, and carries the\n   kit's theme toggle with id `theme-toggle`, usable at both widths.\n4. A footer that belongs to JobyCorp.\n5. The landing page: a hero that says what JobyCorp does in one sentence, a\n   section on the research (what is measured and how), a section on the\n   hardware and method (local models, local hardware, results published in\n   full), and a closing call to action to read the research. Sections are\n   yours to add or merge; every section must earn its place.\n6. At least one composite component of your own, registered in the\n   DesignManifest with a preview (host composites show on\n   `/custom-designs`), used on more than one page.\n\n## Design requirements\n\n- Light and dark themes, both finished, with the palette `DESIGN.md`\n  defines applied to the `light` and `dark` themes in `app.css` (keep\n  those two names; the theme toggle switches by them). Phone and desktop,\n  both finished. No horizontal overflow at 390 px. Body text contrast at\n  least 4.5:1 and large text at least 3:1 in both themes.\n- The installed heroicon set is `deps/heroicons/optimized/24/outline`\n  (and `solid`); the name is `hero-` plus the file name without `.svg`.\n- `Layouts.app` and a LiveView's `render/1` are exempt from the lint's\n  unmarked-component rule. `mix format` (part of precommit) re-indents\n  HEEx — re-read a block before editing it after a format.\n- Every icon name you use must exist in the installed heroicon set; check\n  before you use it. A blank icon is a defect.\n- Copy is concise: headings of a few words, sentences a visitor can read\n  at a glance. Copy is about JobyCorp and its research, never about the\n  component kit, the framework, or this task.\n- Compose the kit's registered wrappers; raw HTML primitives are a lint\n  failure. Lint must be clean.\n\n## Tests\n\n7. Existing tests must pass; update any test that referred to removed\n   demo content. No new features. Add a render test for each new page.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The dev server must run on port 4099; `PORT` is already set. Do not use\n  any other port. Do not stop or kill processes you did not " <> ..., ~U[2026-09-11 08:30:36.486139Z], "34a9c88e-ed51-4813-a8a3-166f7387f1d9"]
