INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_call_id","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{"duration_ms" => 1, "ok" => true, "tool" => "read"}, 7, :tool, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "[benchapp/DESIGN.md: 240 lines, showing 1–240]\n1\t# DESIGN.md — JobyCorp\n2\t\n3\tThis is the design direction for the JobyCorp site. It is one direction,\n4\tshared by everyone who builds the site. Where the brief and this file\n5\tdiffer, the brief wins. Where this file is silent, use judgment and keep\n6\tto its spirit: an instrument, not a brochure — and not a document\n7\teither.\n8\t\n9\t## Who this is for\n10\t\n11\tJobyCorp runs analysis and benchmarks of local LLMs on its own hardware\n12\tand publishes the work in full. The visitor is technical, skeptical, and\n13\tshort on time. They have seen a hundred AI company sites and trust none\n14\tof them. This one earns trust by looking like the work: exact, modern,\n15\tand confident — a well-made instrument that someone clearly cared about.\n16\tIt should feel technical, not clinical. A plain page of paragraphs is a\n17\tfailure of this brief as much as a page of gradient blobs is.\n18\t\n19\t## The one idea\n20\t\n21\tMeasurement is the subject, so measurement is the look. The site has\n22\ttwo voices: a sans for reading and a monospace for anything measured —\n23\tfield names, units, model identifiers, tables. The monospace voice is\n24\tnot decoration; it marks the places where a visitor is looking at data.\n25\t\n26\tThe memorable object is the **record card** in the hero: beside the\n27\tone-sentence statement of what JobyCorp does sits a specimen of a\n28\tJobyCorp run record — the fields a record carries and the unit each\n29\tquantity is reported in — set in monospace on a plotting-paper surface\n30\t(a faint grid drawn in CSS), framed by the accent. Field names and\n31\tunits only, never invented values. The same card, or a sibling of it,\n32\tappears on the research page. That is where the boldness is spent;\n33\teverything around it is disciplined.\n34\t\n35\tEvery page carries at least one figure — a record card, a table, a\n36\tspecimen block. Prose alone is not a page.\n37\t\n38\t## What to avoid\n39\t\n40\tThese are the marks of generated design. None of them appear.\n41\t\n42\t- Gradient text, gradient headline words, gradient buttons, gradient\n43\t  washes as backgrounds. Blurred colour blobs behind a hero.\n44\t  Backdrop-blur headers, glassmorphism, glows, soft drop shadows.\n45\t- A cream or parchment page with a terracotta accent. A black page with\n46\t  an acid-green accent. A tinted near-black (`#0B0B0B`, `#111`) for\n47\t  black.\n48\t- Content chopped into identical rounded cards with one radius and one\n49\t  shadow. A panel exists to hold a figure or a table, not to box prose.\n50\t- Three identical items in a row with an icon, a bold title, and two\n51\t  lines. Icon tiles. An icon per feature. Emoji, sparkles, rockets.\n52\t- A tracked-out ALL-CAPS label above every heading. Meta strings joined\n53\t  with middle dots. A `→` appended to link or button text. One word in a\n54\t  headline set in another colour or style.\n55\t- Numbered markers on content that is not a sequence. JobyCorp's method\n56\t  *is* a sequence and may be numbered.\n57\t- Badges and pills that announce nothing. Stock illustration, isometric\n58\t  scenes, 3D shapes, hero photos of hardware.\n59\t- Motion: entrances on scroll, fades, hover lifts. Nothing moves unless\n60\t  the visitor did something.\n61\t- Copy that could be about any company: \"Unleash\", \"Supercharge\",\n62\t  \"Seamless\", \"Cutting-edge\", \"Empower\", \"Next-generation\",\n63\t  \"Revolutionary\", \"Effortless\", \"Elevate\", \"Robust\", \"Leverage\",\n64\t  \"Harness\", \"Delightful\", \"Blazing\", \"Trusted by\". Exclamation marks.\n65\t  Questions as headings.\n66\t- Numbers invented to look impressive. Where there is no real number,\n67\t  the figure shows the field and its unit, and the sentence does not\n68\t  need one.\n69\t\n70\t## Layout\n71\t\n72\t- Content column `max-w-6xl`, centred on the page, contents\n73\t  left-aligned. `px-6` at phone width, `px-8` from `md`. Prose inside it\n74\t  keeps a reading measure of `max-w-prose`; figures and tables may use\n75\t  the full column.\n76\t- The hero is two columns from `lg`: the statement on the left (the\n77\t  sentence, one paragraph, the primary action), the record card on the\n78\t  right, top-aligned. At phone" <> ..., "chatcmpl-tool-aac981dc157e8cfc", ~U[2026-09-11 08:30:53.928583Z], "b808dd84-50c3-407e-82a8-61c9969e5e42"]
