INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_call_id","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{"duration_ms" => 2, "ok" => true, "tool" => "read"}, 26, :tool, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "[benchapp/deps/joby_kit/lib/joby_kit/core_components.ex: 1180 lines, showing 1–1180]\n1\tdefmodule JobyKit.CoreComponents do\n2\t  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n3\t  Core wrapper components shipped by JobyKit. Each component:\n4\t\n5\t    * Carries `data-component=\"JobyKit.CoreComponents.<name>\"` on its\n6\t      root element.\n7\t    * Declares every prop with `attr` (variant/size enums via `values:`).\n8\t    * Accepts `attr :rest, :global` so callers can pass id/class/aria-*/\n9\t      phx-* through.\n10\t    * Composes daisyUI primitives + theme tokens internally; the `class`\n11\t      attr (where exposed) is **additive**, layered on top of the\n12\t      wrapper's identity classes.\n13\t\n14\t  Hosts register these against `JobyKit.CoreComponents` in their\n15\t  manifest:\n16\t\n17\t      component JobyKit.CoreComponents, :button,\n18\t        category: :core,\n19\t        daisy_basis: \"btn\",\n20\t        summary: \"Standard text button.\",\n21\t        preview: &MyAppWeb.DesignPreviews.button_preview/1\n22\t\n23\t  And expose them by `import`ing this module into their `core_components`\n24\t  / `html_helpers` (or `_web.ex`) so call sites can use the `<.button>`\n25\t  form.\n26\t\n27\t  ## Components\n28\t\n29\t    * `flash/1`, `flash_group/1` — toast-style flashes\n30\t    * `badge/1` — status chip with a semantic tone\n31\t    * `button/1` — text/link button with variant, size, and shape\n32\t    * `card/1` — content surface with eyebrow/title/actions slots\n33\t    * `eyebrow/1` — small uppercase label\n34\t    * `header/1` — page or section header\n35\t    * `icon/1` — Heroicon span\n36\t    * `input/1` — form input (text, email, select, textarea, checkbox…)\n37\t    * `list/1` — generic list\n38\t    * `modal/1` — server-driven dialog\n39\t    * `table/1` — table with col/action slots, stream-aware\n40\t    * `theme_toggle/1` — system / light / dark control\n41\t\n42\t  Plus the JS helpers `show/2`, `hide/2`, and the i18n-free\n43\t  `translate_error/1`.\n44\t  \"\"\"\n45\t\n46\t  use Phoenix.Component\n47\t\n48\t  alias Phoenix.LiveView.JS\n49\t\n50\t  # --------------------------------------------------------------- icon\n51\t\n52\t  @doc \"\"\"\n53\t  Renders a [Heroicon](https://heroicons.com).\n54\t\n55\t  Heroicons come in three styles — outline, solid, and mini. Default is\n56\t  outline; pass `name=\"hero-foo-solid\"` or `name=\"hero-foo-mini\"` for the\n57\t  others. The host must have the Heroicons CSS plugin installed (Phoenix\n58\t  ships this by default in `assets/vendor/heroicons.js`).\n59\t\n60\t      <.icon name=\"hero-x-mark\" />\n61\t      <.icon name=\"hero-arrow-path\" class=\"ml-1 size-3 motion-safe:animate-spin\" />\n62\t  \"\"\"\n63\t  attr :name, :string, required: true\n64\t  attr :class, :any, default: \"size-4\"\n65\t  attr :rest, :global\n66\t\n67\t  def icon(%{name: \"hero-\" <> _} = assigns) do\n68\t    ~H\"\"\"\n69\t    <span data-component=\"JobyKit.CoreComponents.icon\" class={[@name, @class]} {@rest} />\n70\t    \"\"\"\n71\t  end\n72\t\n73\t  # Without this the caller gets a bare FunctionClauseError pointing at\n74\t  # the kit, which says nothing about the actual mistake.\n75\t  def icon(%{name: name}) do\n76\t    raise ArgumentError, \"\"\"\n77\t    unknown icon \#{inspect(name)}.\n78\t\n79\t    `<.icon>` renders Heroicons, whose names start with \"hero-\". Try\n80\t    \#{inspect(\"hero-\" <> to_string(name))}, or browse https://heroicons.com.\n81\t    \"\"\"\n82\t  end\n83\t\n84\t  # ------------------------------------------------------------- button\n85\t\n86\t  @doc \"\"\"\n87\t  Standard text button. Renders as `<button>` by default, or `<.link>`\n88\t  when `href`/`navigate`/`patch` is passed via `:rest`.\n89\t\n90\t      <.button>Send</.button>\n91\t      <.button variant=\"primary\" size=\"sm\">Save</.button>\n92\t      <.button navigate={~p\"/dashboard\"}>Home</.button>\n93\t\n94\t  `type` passes through, so a non-submitting button inside a form is\n95\t  `<.button type=\"button\">`. Omitted, the browser default applies —\n96\t  `submit` inside a form.\n97\t\n98\t  ## Tone\n99\t\n100\t  `variant` carries meaning, not just colour — `danger` is how a\n101\t  destructive action reads as destructive:\n102\t\n103\t      <.button variant=\"danger\">Delete workspace</.button>\n104\t      <.button variant=\"ghost\">Dismiss</.button>\n105\t\n106\t  The d" <> ..., "chatcmpl-tool-819e9bb4907eb198", ~U[2026-09-11 08:31:34.239658Z], "45794d68-4265-4613-a04b-716d7afb925a"]
