INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{}, 37, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", [%{"arguments" => %{"command" => "cd /Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp && for i in bars-3 bars-4 bars-2 x-mark sun moon computer-desktop; do [ -f deps/heroicons/optimized/24/outline/$i.svg ] && echo \"OK outline/$i\" || echo \"MISS $i\"; done"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-a133c980b254aa5f", "name" => "bash"}], "Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me set up a todo plan and start building. Let me also quickly verify the heroicons I want to use exist, and check app.js and the mix.exs / precommit alias.\n\nLet me plan the build:\n\n1. **app.css** — replace `light` and `dark` themes with the DESIGN.md palette. Add a `.plotting-paper` CSS class (grid with repeating-linear-gradient), radius/border/depth tokens. Add link hover transition.\n\n2. **Layouts.app** (`layouts.ex`) — custom nav with `main-nav`, `nav-toggle`, `theme-toggle`, current page aria-current, phone collapse. Remove stock simple_nav, remove \"built with\" footer and design links. New footer belonging to JobyCorp. Need a JS toggle for the nav at phone width — but no inline scripts allowed. I can use a checkbox hack (daisyUI) or use LiveView JS commands. Actually the toggle button `nav-toggle` — I can use `Phoenix.LiveView.JS` toggle on click via `phx-click`. But `Layouts.app` render... it's a function component; phx-click works inside LiveView render since it's rendered within the LiveView. Yes — `JS.toggle(to: \"#main-nav-menu\")` via phx-click works in a function component rendered by a LiveView. Good, that avoids custom JS.\n\n   The theme-toggle id: the kit's theme_toggle has data-component and a join div. The brief wants `id=\"theme-toggle\"` — I can pass `id` via rest to theme_toggle? theme_toggle has `attr :rest, :global` so `<JobyKit.CoreComponents.theme_toggle id=\"theme-toggle\" />` puts id on root. Good.\n\n3. **Router** — add `/research` ResearchLive, `/about` AboutLive routes.\n\n4. **HomeLive** — rewrite: hero (statement + record card), research section, hardware/method section, CTA.\n\n5. **ResearchLive** — what JobyCorp publishes and how it tests. Include a table (figures) + a record-card sibling.\n\n6. **AboutLive** — who and why.\n\n7. **CompositeComponents** — a `record_card` composite (used on home hero + research page) — meets \"composite used on more than one page\". Register in DesignManifest with preview in DesignPreviews.\n\n8. **DesignManifest** — register record_card. Keep empty_state? It's a demo component referencing inbox/teammate (demo content). The brief says remove demo content traces. The empty_state is \"the worked example\" from the generator. I'll remove empty_state (it's generator demo) and replace with my own composite. Actually removing it requires removing its preview + manifest entry. Let me just replace it entirely with my record_card composite to keep it clean. But lint's unregistered rules: empty_state references \"inbox\"/\"teammate\" — that's demo content, remove it.\n\n9. **Tests** — render test for each new page (home, research, about). Update error tests? They're fine. Add tests for the pages.\n\nLet me first verify heroicons names I'll use. DESIGN says only theme toggle + nav toggle icons; \"no others\". So I should avoid feature icons. Nav toggle typically uses `hero-bars-3` and `hero-x-mark`. Those are part of \"nav toggle\" so allowed. Let me verify names exist.\n\nThe nav-toggle icon: bars-3. Let me check. Also I'll need to be careful about \"A trailing `→` on links\" - avoid.\n\nLet me start writing. I'll keep it disciplined and match DESIGN.md closely.\n\nFor the nav toggle without custom JS: daisyUI has `lg:` classes. I'll use phx-click JS toggle on the menu. Let me design:\n\n```\n<header id=\"main-nav\" class=\"sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-base-300 bg-base-100\">\n  <div class=\"mx-auto flex max-w-6xl items-center justify-between gap-6 px-6 py-4 md:px-8\">\n    <.link navigate=\"/\" wordmark>\n    <nav class=\"hidden md:flex ...\">links</nav>  <!-- desktop -->\n    <div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\">\n      theme_toggle\n      <button id=\"nav-toggle\" class=\"md:hidden\" phx-click={JS.toggle(to: \"#mobile-menu\")}>icon</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"mobile-menu\" class=\"md:hidden hidden ...\">links</div>\n</header>\n```\n\nWait — `JS.toggle` with display. `JS.toggle(to: \"#mobile-menu\", ins: \"...\", ...)` or just `in: \"hidden\"`? Actually toggle: `JS.toggle(to: \"#mobile-menu\")` toggles display via inline style + attributes. Simpler: use `JS.toggle(to: \"#mobile-menu\", d" <> ..., ~U[2026-09-11 08:33:18.245588Z], "968afa4b-3ea2-4ed7-9400-58c71f39c31f"]
