INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 41, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nI now have a complete picture. Let me set up the plan and start building.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"action" => "add", "items" => ["Apply DESIGN.md palette to light/dark themes + plotting-paper/wordmark CSS in app.css", "Rewrite Layouts.app: main-nav, nav-toggle, theme-toggle, aria-current, JobyCorp footer", "Add /research and /about routes", "Add composites (record_card, spec_row) + register in manifest + previews", "Rewrite HomeLive (hero+record card, research, hardware/method, CTA)", "Build ResearchLive", "Build AboutLive", "Add render tests per page", "Run mix precommit + joby_kit.lint, fix issues", "Preview all pages 1440/390 both themes, no overflow"]}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-8913fa064f23775e", "name" => "todo"}], "I have a comprehensive understanding now. Let me set up a plan and start building.\n\nPlan:\n1. app.css — replace theme tokens with DESIGN.md palette; add `.plotting-paper` grid class; add link/button hover transition; wordmark mark. Set radius/border/depth tokens.\n2. layouts.ex — rewrite `app/1`: custom nav with main-nav, nav-toggle, theme-toggle, aria-current, footer for JobyCorp. Need active_nav passed from each page.\n3. router.ex — add /research and /about routes.\n4. HomeLive — rewrite: hero with statement + record card, research section, hardware/method section, CTA.\n5. ResearchLive — new.\n6. AboutLive — new.\n7. CompositeComponents — add a composite (e.g. `record_card` and/or `spec_row`) used on more than one page. Register in DesignManifest + preview in DesignPreviews.\n8. Remove empty_state demo? The brief says remove welcome content of HomeLive and demo traces. The empty_state is a worked example composite. It's referenced in design_previews + manifest. I'll replace it with my own composite. But `/custom-designs` shows host composites — fine, keep it registered but swap demo for my composite. Actually I should remove the demo empty_state (it's \"the generator's demo\"). But empty_state isn't linked from the site; it only shows on /custom-designs which is not linked. The brief says remove welcome content of HomeLive, stock nav, built-with footer, and links to /design etc. The empty_state composite is generator's worked example but not linked on the site. I can replace it with my own composite to be clean. Let me replace empty_state with my own composites (record_card + spec_row) — remove empty_state and its preview to remove demo traces.\n\nActually, safer: keep empty_state removed, register my composite(s). DesignManifest references CompositeComponents.empty_state & DesignPreviews.empty_state_preview. I'll replace those.\n\nThe composite must be used on more than one page. My composite: `spec_row`? Let me think about which composite. DESIGN.md: \"record card ... The same card, or a sibling of it, appears on the research page.\" So the record card is a great composite to register and use on home + research. Let me make `record_card` a composite. It renders a monospace list of fields+units on a plotting-paper surface with caption. Used on home hero and research page.\n\nAlso a `spec_row` (monospace label + reading value) is used on home + research + about — that's also a good composite used across pages. I'll make record_card the primary registered composite (required: registered in DesignManifest with a preview, used on more than one page). I can also add spec_row as another registered composite. Both fine.\n\nLet me keep it focused: register `record_card` (composite, preview, used home+research). That satisfies req #6. I might add a second composite `spec_row` used across all three pages for the spec-sheet layout — good for avoiding raw duplicated markup too.\n\nLet me design the composite components carefully with the wrapper contract (attr, data-component, attr :rest :global, compose core wrappers, registered).\n\nrecord_card:\n- attrs: title (field name list?) Better: accept a `fields` list attr of `%{field: name, unit: unit}`, plus `title`/`caption`. Render on plotting-paper. This is data (fields + units), no invented values.\n\nLet me make it:\n```\nattr :fields, :list, required: true  # [%{field:, unit:}]\nattr :title, :string, default: \"run record\"\nattr :caption, :string, default: nil\nattr :rest, :global\n```\nRoot: div with plotting-paper class, data-component. Uses CoreComponents inside? The plotting-paper is a custom surface. The composite wraps it. Inside I render field rows. The composite's internals should compose core wrappers where possible; but this is mostly typography/figures. The lint raw_html_primitive only flags button/input/textarea/select. div/span/table/etc are fine raw (page-level). But \"unmarked_component\" — the record_card def carries data-component so it's fine.\n\nFor fields, I could use `<CoreComponents.list>` but I want mono alignment label/value. I'll just render raw divs inside the wrapper — allowed.\n\nLet me a" <> ..., ~U[2026-09-11 08:34:13.843326Z], "cba7a87b-3fed-48db-9cea-802a4a546ed7"]
