INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 47, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nNow the composites. Let me write `composite_components.ex` with `record_card` and `spec_row`.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"content" => "defmodule BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Generic, multi-primitive composites for this app.\n\n  Composites live one layer above core wrappers: they bundle a small set\n  of `JobyKit.CoreComponents` primitives and theme tokens into a\n  higher-level pattern that appears more than once across the site.\n\n  Every composite follows the JobyKit wrapper contract:\n\n    1. Declare every prop with `attr` (use `values:` for variant enums).\n    2. Carry `data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.<name>\"`\n       on the root element.\n    3. Accept `attr :rest, :global` for id/class/aria-*/phx-* pass-through.\n    4. Internals compose theme tokens and the plotting-paper surface —\n       never raw `<button>`/`<input>`/`<textarea>`.\n    5. Register the composite in `BenchappWeb.DesignManifest`\n       (`category: :composite`) so it surfaces on `/custom-designs` and\n       in `/design.json`.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use BenchappWeb, :html\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  A JobyCorp run record shown as a specimen: the fields a record carries\n  and the unit each quantity is reported in, set in monospace on a\n  plotting-paper surface framed by the accent trace. Field names and\n  units only — never invented values. An optional caption sits under the\n  card in the secondary text colour.\n\n      <.record_card\n        title=\"run record\"\n        fields={[\n          %{field: \"model\", unit: \"id\"},\n          %{field: \"ttft\", unit: \"ms\"}\n        ]}\n        caption=\"What every published run carries.\"\n      />\n  \"\"\"\n  attr :fields, :list, required: true, doc: \"List of `%{field:, unit:}` maps.\"\n  attr :title, :string, default: \"run record\"\n  attr :caption, :string, default: nil, doc: \"One-line caption beneath the card.\"\n  attr :class, :any, default: nil\n  attr :rest, :global\n\n  def record_card(assigns) do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <div data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.record_card\" class={@class} {@rest}>\n      <div class=\"plotting-paper rounded-box p-6\">\n        <div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-secondary/40 pb-2\">\n          <span class=\"font-mono text-sm text-base-content\">{@title}</span>\n          <span class=\"font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-base-content/70\">\n            record\n          </span>\n        </div>\n        <dl class=\"pt-1 font-mono text-sm\">\n          <div\n            :for={f <- @fields}\n            class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-b border-secondary/20 py-1.5 last:border-0\"\n          >\n            <dt class=\"text-base-content\">{f.field}</dt>\n            <dd class=\"text-base-content/70\">{f.unit}</dd>\n          </div>\n        </dl>\n      </div>\n      <p :if={@caption} class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-base-content/70\">\n        {@caption}\n      </p>\n    </div>\n    \"\"\"\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  A spec-sheet row: a monospace label in a fixed column beside a reading\n  column. From `md` the two sit side by side; at phone width they stack.\n  Use several in a `space-y-*` container to build a spec sheet.\n\n      <.spec_row label=\"method\">\n        Each model is loaded and run locally, on hardware we own.\n      </.spec_row>\n  \"\"\"\n  attr :label, :string, required: true, doc: \"Monospace label in the fixed column.\"\n  attr :class, :any, default: nil\n  attr :rest, :global\n  slot :inner_block, required: true, doc: \"Reading column content.\"\n\n  def spec_row(assigns) do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <div\n      data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.spec_row\"\n      class={[\"border-t border-base-300 pt-4 md:flex md:gap-8\", @class]}\n      {@rest}\n    >\n      <dt class=\"w-44 shrink-0 pb-1 font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70 md:pb-0\">\n        {@label}\n      </dt>\n      <dd class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed\">{render_slot(@inner_block)}</dd>\n    </div>\n    \"\"\"\n  end\nend\n", "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/lib/benchapp_web/components/composite_components.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-b92371e08c574e13", "name" => "write"}], "Now let me build the composites. Let me design the composite components:\n\n1. `record_card` — the plotting-paper record card. Fields with units. Used on home hero + research page.\n2. `spec_row` — the monospace label column beside a reading column. Used on home (method), about, research. Good candidate for \"composite used on more than one page\".\n\nBoth will be composites registered in the manifest with previews.\n\nLet me think about the record_card structure:\n- attr `title` (the record type), `fields` (list of %{field, unit} maps), `caption`\n- root div with plotting-paper + rounded-box + p-6, data-component, attr :rest\n- inside: a monospace list of field: unit pairs\n- caption under it in secondary text\n\nThe DESIGN.md says: \"the fields a record carries and the unit each quantity is reported in — set in monospace on a plotting-paper surface... Field names and units only, never invented values.\"\n\nSo a field like `ttft` → `ms`, `throughput` → `tokens/s`, `hardware` → `device`, `model` → `id`, `seed` → `int`, `tokens` → `count`, etc.\n\nspec_row:\n- attr `label` (mono, w-44, text-sm secondary), content slot (reading column)\n- root: div flex flex-col md:flex-row, label + content. data-component. attr :rest.\n\nLet me write the composite components file. I'll rewrite composite_components.ex entirely, replacing empty_state with these two (remove empty_state — the brief says remove demo; empty_state is a generator worked example. I should remove it to remove \"every trace of the generator's demo\"? The empty_state is a demo worked example. To be safe and clean, I'll remove empty_state and its preview, replacing with my own composites. That also means removing the manifest entry + preview.)\n\nNow design the data-component values:\n- `BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.record_card`\n- `BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.spec_row`\n\nLet me write composite_components.ex.\n\nFor record_card, I want the fields rendered as a definition list style with dotted leaders maybe. Keep it clean: each row `field` left in mono, `unit` right in mono secondary. Use border-b hairlines between rows (base-300). Let me design:\n\n```\n<div data-component=... class=\"plotting-paper rounded-box p-6 font-mono text-sm\" {@rest}>\n  <div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-secondary/30 pb-2 mb-1 text-secondary\">\n    <span>{@title}</span>\n    <span class=\"text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-base-content/70\">record</span>\n  </div>\n  <dl class=\"divide-y divide-secondary/15\">\n    <div :for={f <- @fields} class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 py-1.5\">\n      <dt class=\"text-base-content\">{f.field}</dt>\n      <dd class=\"text-base-content/70\">{f.unit}</dd>\n    </div>\n  </dl>\n</div>\n```\nWait — DESIGN says secondary is \"never text\". So the field names should be base-content, units maybe base-content/70. The title could be secondary though? It says secondary \"never text\". So avoid text-secondary entirely. Let me make the header row text in base-content and the small label base-content/70. Good.\n\nActually I want the frame/grid to be the secondary trace. The header hairline can be `border-secondary/40` (a mark, that's fine — it's a rule not text). Good.\n\nThe caption should be outside the plotting-paper card, under it, in secondary text color (base-content/70). But if caption is a slot inside the composite root, it'd be inside the plot surface. Better: the composite root is a column wrap (truncated)
