INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 59, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nNow add the routes.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "    live \"/\", HomeLive, :index\n    live \"/research\", ResearchLive, :index\n    live \"/about\", AboutLive, :index\n    live \"/design\", DesignSystemLive, :index\n    live \"/custom-designs\", CustomDesignsLive, :index", "old_string" => "    live \"/\", HomeLive, :index\n    live \"/design\", DesignSystemLive, :index\n    live \"/custom-designs\", CustomDesignsLive, :index", "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/lib/benchapp_web/router.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-90bfac5cfad8e3cc", "name" => "edit"}], "The `.button` uses `id=\"nav-toggle\"` via :rest global (id is in :global). Good. But wait — does the `shape=\"square\"` button with `class=\"md:hidden\"` — the class is additive on root. The button root is `<button class=\"btn btn-ghost btn-square md:hidden\">`. Good, hidden on desktop.\n\nBut the nav-toggle button uses `phx-click` with a JS command. That's fine since it's within a LiveView render context (the Layouts.app is rendered inside LiveView). Good.\n\nOne concern: The `.button` component's rest :global includes id via global — yes :global includes id, aria-*, etc. Actually :global default includes standard HTML attributes including id, aria-* (aria-* are always allowed by global? Phoenix's `:global` includes aria-* and data-* and standard attributes). Let me recall: Phoenix.Component `attr :rest, :global` — the `:global` type allows attributes that are in Phoenix.HTML's global attributes list, plus `aria-*` and `data-*` are allowed via wildcard? Actually global rest passes anything that is a \"global\" HTML attribute (like id, class, aria-*, data-*, role, etc. — specifically a known list plus aria-/data- prefix). id is allowed. aria-controls, aria-expanded, aria-label are allowed (aria-*). type — the button component's rest includes `type` explicitly in its include list. Good. phx-click — phx-* are allowed via global? Phoenix LiveView extends global to include phx-*. Yes when LiveView is loaded, `phx-*` are added to allowed global attributes. Good.\n\nNow the button also declares its own `attr :class` and I'm passing class — fine. But I'm passing `id` and `aria-*` and `phx-click` which go to rest. Good.\n\nNow update the router to add /research and /about.\n\nLet me also reconsider: the theme_toggle button — it passes `id=\"theme-toggle\"` to theme_toggle which has `attr :rest, :global`. Good, id lands on root div. Good.\n\nNow, DESIGN.md says no backdrop-blur on header — I used solid bg-base-100, good. Sticky is fine (browser default, not motion entrance).\n\nNow the router.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:39:58.234385Z], "3c69e2c6-b1ad-4f3c-a22c-620c55298947"]
