INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 61, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nNow make the composites available app-wide by importing them in `benchapp_web.ex`.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "      # JobyKit-shipped wrappers: <.button>, <.card>, <.icon>, <.input>,\n      # <.flash>, <.flash_group>, <.header>, <.list>, <.table>.\n      import JobyKit.CoreComponents\n\n      # This app's registered composites: <.record_card>, <.spec_row>.\n      import BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents", "old_string" => "      # JobyKit-shipped wrappers: <.button>, <.card>, <.icon>, <.input>,\n      # <.flash>, <.flash_group>, <.header>, <.list>, <.table>.\n      import JobyKit.CoreComponents", "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/lib/benchapp_web.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-81320b23114586c2", "name" => "edit"}], "Now I need to import CompositeComponents into html_helpers so `<.record_card>` and `<.spec_row>` work in LiveViews. Let me add to benchapp_web.ex html_helpers. But that could cause the lint forked_wrapper rule? No. It imports BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents. The lint's forked_wrapper only checks `import JobyKit.CoreComponents, except:`. Fine.\n\nHowever, there's a concern: importing CompositeComponents globally means `use BenchappWeb, :html` in CompositeComponents itself would import itself — harmless, but the lint `unmarked_component` scan: composite_components.ex defs have data-component (they carry data-component) so they're \"wrapper_line_ranges\" → exempt from unmarked. Good.\n\nAlso importing CompositeComponents means `<.record_card>` available in DesignPreviews too (which uses full `CompositeComponents.record_card`). Both fine.\n\nLet me add the import.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:40:12.488761Z], "fbade964-ea6e-4c14-a397-5e8a1022310b"]
