INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 63, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nNow the landing page. Let me write `HomeLive`.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"content" => "defmodule BenchappWeb.HomeLive do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  The JobyCorp landing page: what we do, what we measure, how a run is\n  done, and where to read it.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use BenchappWeb, :live_view\n\n  @record_fields [\n    %{field: \"model\", unit: \"id\"},\n    %{field: \"quantization\", unit: \"preset\"},\n    %{field: \"prompt tokens\", unit: \"count\"},\n    %{field: \"generated tokens\", unit: \"count\"},\n    %{field: \"ttft\", unit: \"ms\"},\n    %{field: \"throughput\", unit: \"tok/s\"},\n    %{field: \"hardware\", unit: \"device\"},\n    %{field: \"seed\", unit: \"int\"}\n  ]\n\n  @measures [\n    %{field: \"ttft\", unit: \"ms\", note: \"Time to the first token, cold.\"},\n    %{field: \"decode\", unit: \"tok/s\", note: \"Tokens generated per second once decoding starts.\"},\n    %{field: \"prompt\", unit: \"tok/s\", note: \"Tokens read per second while the prompt is processed.\"},\n    %{field: \"peak\", unit: \"MiB\", note: \"Resident memory held by the running model.\"}\n  ]\n\n  @impl true\n  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n    {:ok,\n     assign(socket,\n       page_title: \"JobyCorp\",\n       record_fields: @record_fields,\n       measures: @measures\n     )}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def render(assigns) do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <Layouts.app flash={@flash} active_nav=\"home\">\n      <div class=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-8\">\n        <section class=\"grid items-start gap-12 py-16 md:py-24 lg:grid-cols-2\">\n          <div class=\"space-y-6\">\n            <h1 class=\"text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.02] tracking-[-0.03em] md:text-7xl\">\n              Local models, measured on local hardware.\n            </h1>\n            <p class=\"max-w-prose text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg\">\n              JobyCorp runs language models on machines we own, measures what they do, and\n              publishes every result in full — fields, units, and method included.\n            </p>\n            <.button navigate={~p\"/research\"} variant=\"primary\" class=\"rounded-field\">\n              Read the research\n            </.button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"lg:pt-2\">\n            <.record_card\n              title=\"run record\"\n              fields={@record_fields}\n              caption=\"What every published run carries.\"\n            />\n          </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"space-y-8 border-t border-base-300 py-16 md:py-24\">\n          <div class=\"flex items-baseline gap-3\">\n            <span class=\"font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70\">measure</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"max-w-prose space-y-3\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl\">What we measure</h2>\n            <p class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg\">\n              Four quantities, measured the same way on every run so results compare across\n              models and machines. The table names each field and the unit it is reported in.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"overflow-x-auto rounded-box border border-base-300\">\n            <.table id=\"measures\" rows={@measures} zebra={false} class=\"[&>thead>tr>th]:bg-base-200\">\n              <:col :let={m} label=\"field\">\n                <span class=\"font-mono text-sm\">{m.field}</span>\n              </:col>\n              <:col :let={m} label=\"unit\">\n                <span class=\"font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70\">{m.unit}</span>\n              </:col>\n              <:col :let={m} label=\"what it captures\">\n                <span class=\"text-sm text-base-content/80\">{m.note}</span>\n              </:col>\n            </.table>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"space-y-8 border-t border-base-300 py-16 md:py-24\">\n          <div class=\"flex items-baseline gap-3\">\n            <span class=\"font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70\">hardware · method</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"max-w-prose space-y-3\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl\">\n              Local by construction\n            </h2>\n            <p class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg\">\n              Nothing in this pipeline" <> ..., "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/lib/benchapp_web/live/home_live.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-84e56d343f4f7510", "name" => "write"}], "Now I've rewritten a lot. Let me build HomeLive. Let me design the copy carefully per DESIGN.md.\n\nFacts: JobyCorp is a local AI research company. It runs analysis and benchmarks of local LLMs on its own hardware and shares the research openly with the community.\n\nHero: one sentence about what JobyCorp does. Something like: \"We run language models on our own hardware, measure them, and publish the results in full.\"\n\nActually the hero statement should be \"one sentence\" big. DESIGN says hero two columns lg: statement left (sentence, one paragraph, primary action), record card right top-aligned.\n\nHero statement (headline, few words): \"Local models, measured on local hardware.\" Then one paragraph, then primary action \"Read the research\" → /research.\n\nRecord card fields (fields + units, never invented values):\n- model — id\n- quantization — preset\n- prompt tokens — count\n- generated tokens — count\n- ttft — ms\n- throughput — tok/s\n- hardware — device\n- seed — int\n- date — iso 8601\n\nGood honest fields.\n\nSections:\n1. Hero\n2. Research — what is measured and how. Use a data section with running head \"measure\". Maybe a table of fields measured with unit + what it means. Table is a figure: bg-base-200 header row, hairlines, numbers right-aligned, identifiers mono.\n3. Hardware and method — local models, local hardware, results published in full. Use spec_row composite (spec sheet). Method is a sequence → can be numbered.\n4. Closing CTA to read research.\n\nEvery section must earn its place. Let me keep: Hero, \"What we measure\" (table), \"How a run is done\" (spec/sequence), \"Read the research\" CTA.\n\nLet me think about sections on landing:\n- Hero (statement + record card)\n- Section: \"What a record carries\" / measurement — the fields. Actually the record card already shows fields. For the research section on the landing, describe what is measured and how — could be prose + a small table of metrics (ttft, throughput, ... with unit and a one-line meaning). That's a figure.\n- Section: hardware & method — spec sheet with spec_row: models, hardware, method, release. Method as a numbered sequence is fine.\n- CTA: read the research.\n\nLet me build HomeLive now. I'll use `.header` for section headings? DESIGN says section headings text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight. The kit `.header` size=\"section\" is text-lg. Not matching. I could use `.header` with title_class to override, or just write headings. Headings are prose not primitives — raw `<h2>` is allowed (lint only flags button/input/textarea/select). But to keep discipline and reuse, I'll write plain `<h2>` with the DESIGN classes. That's fine — headings aren't a primitive with a wrapper; `.header` is the wrapper though. Hmm. The kit has `<.header>`. But its type scale (text-lg) doesn't match DESIGN's section heading (text-3xl). I can pass `size=\"page\"` (text-3xl) + title_class for md:text-4xl. But header wraps subtitle in text-sm text-base-content/70; DESIGN body is larger. For section intros I want a lead paragraph text-base md:text-lg. \n\nI think writing semantic `<h2>`/`<p>` directly is  (truncated)
