INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 65, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nNow the research and about pages.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"content" => "defmodule BenchappWeb.ResearchLive do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  What JobyCorp publishes and how each run is tested.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use BenchappWeb, :live_view\n\n  @release_fields [\n    %{field: \"model\", unit: \"id\"},\n    %{field: \"prompts\", unit: \"set id\"},\n    %{field: \"seeds\", unit: \"count\"},\n    %{field: \"ttft\", unit: \"ms\"},\n    %{field: \"decode\", unit: \"tok/s\"},\n    %{field: \"peak\", unit: \"MiB\"},\n    %{field: \"method\", unit: \"version\"}\n  ]\n\n  @method [\n    \"Pin the model to a fixed revision and the runtime to a fixed build.\",\n    \"Fix the prompts, seeds, and metrics before the first run — never chosen after.\",\n    \"Load and run locally, on hardware named in the record.\",\n    \"Record every field from the run itself; nothing is filled in later.\",\n    \"Publish the full record, so the result can be checked or reproduced.\"\n  ]\n\n  @fixed [\n    %{field: \"prompts\", fixed_by: \"a named set, shared with the results\"},\n    %{field: \"seeds\", fixed_by: \"chosen before the run and listed per result\"},\n    %{field: \"revision\", fixed_by: \"a pinned model and runtime build\"},\n    %{field: \"device\", fixed_by: \"named in every record\"},\n    %{field: \"metrics\", fixed_by: \"the same four, measured the same way\"}\n  ]\n\n  @impl true\n  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n    {:ok,\n     assign(socket,\n       page_title: \"Research\",\n       release_fields: @release_fields,\n       method: @method,\n       fixed: @fixed\n     )}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def render(assigns) do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <Layouts.app flash={@flash} active_nav=\"research\">\n      <div class=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-8\">\n        <section class=\"grid items-start gap-12 py-16 md:py-24 lg:grid-cols-2\">\n          <div class=\"space-y-5\">\n            <h1 class=\"text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.03em] md:text-6xl\">\n              How a run is published\n            </h1>\n            <p class=\"max-w-prose text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg\">\n              We publish the record, not a summary of it. Each release bundles the fields a run\n              was measured on, so a reader can check the method or run it again themselves.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"lg:pt-2\">\n            <.record_card\n              title=\"release record\"\n              fields={@release_fields}\n              caption=\"What a published release bundles.\"\n            />\n          </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"space-y-8 border-t border-base-300 py-16 md:py-24\">\n          <div class=\"flex items-baseline gap-3\">\n            <span class=\"font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70\">method</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"max-w-prose space-y-3\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl\">How a run is tested</h2>\n            <p class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg\">\n              One protocol, applied the same way every time. The steps run in order; each one is\n              fixed before the next begins.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n          <ol class=\"max-w-prose divide-y divide-base-300 border-t border-base-300\">\n            <li\n              :for={{step, index} <- Enum.with_index(@method, 1)}\n              class=\"flex gap-4 py-4\"\n            >\n              <span class=\"w-6 shrink-0 font-mono text-sm text-primary\">{:io_lib.format(\"~2..0B\", [index])}</span>\n              <span class=\"text-base leading-relaxed md:text-lg\">{step}</span>\n            </li>\n          </ol>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"space-y-8 border-t border-base-300 py-16 md:py-24\">\n          <div class=\"flex items-baseline gap-3\">\n            <span class=\"font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70\">held fixed</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"max-w-prose space-y-3\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl\">What stays the same</h2>\n            <p class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg\">\n              Comparisons only mean something when everything except the model is held fixed.\n              Each input is named and shared alongside the result" <> ..., "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/lib/benchapp_web/live/research_live.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-ad5ee31022d0bf31", "name" => "write"}], "Now ResearchLive and AboutLive. Let me write ResearchLive: what JobyCorp publishes and how it tests.\n\nDESIGN.md: \"Every page carries at least one figure — a record card, a table, a specimen block.\" Research page should show a sibling of the record card + a table + numbered method sequence (method is a sequence, allowed to be numbered).\n\nLet me build ResearchLive:\n- Section intro: \"What we publish and how a run is tested.\"\n- A figure: a \"published run\" specimen — use record_card sibling (sibling = same composite, different fields: a published release record). Fields: model id, prompt set, seeds count, ttft ms, decode tok/s, peak MiB, method version, released date? date is invented... avoid dates. Use fields+units only, never invented values. So a \"release record\" card listing what a release bundles.\n- The method (numbered sequence): numbered markers ARE allowed since method is a sequence. But DESIGN warns against \"numbered markers on content that is not a sequence.\" Method IS a sequence → may be numbered. I could use `<.list>` but that doesn't number. Or a simple ordered presentation. Let me present the method as an ordered set. I'll do a plain `<ol>` with mono numbers. But raw `<ol>/<li>` is fine (not a primitive). Numbering method: pin model → fix prompts/seeds → run → record → publish. That's a genuine sequence.\n- Table: \"how it's tested\" — stages with a column of what's held fixed. Or reuse the record fields.\n\nLet me design a clean Research page:\n1. Hero-ish header (not full hero; DESIGN prose sections open with heading). A top section with an h1 \"How a run is published\" + intro paragraph + a record_card (sibling) as the figure, two-col at lg. Actually the record card is bold; put one figure here.\n2. \"The method\" — numbered sequence (ol).\n3. \"What a release contains\" — a table (fields a release carries) — but that overlaps record card. Alternatively a table of \"what is held fixed across runs\" (field | value source). Hmm.\n\nLet me keep it: \n- Section 1: heading + para + record_card (the \"release record\" sibling) as figure (two-col lg).\n- Section 2: \"How a run is tested\" numbered method (ol, numbered markers OK).\n- Section 3: \"What we hold fixed\" — a table with columns: field | unit | fixed by. Rows: prompts, seed, hardware, revision, metrics.\n\nThat's three sections, each earns place, has figures (card + table), plus numbered sequence. Good.\n\nFor the record_card sibling on research: title \"release record\", fields = what a release bundles: %{field:\"model\", unit:\"id\"}, %{\"prompts\", \"set id\"}, %{\"seeds\", \"count\"}, %{\"ttft\", \"ms\"}, %{\"decode\", \"tok/s\"}, %{\"peak\", \"MiB\"}, %{\"method\", \"version\"}. caption: \"What a published release bundles.\"\n\nNow numbered method sequence. DESIGN: method is a sequence and may be numbered. Let me use an `<ol>` with mono index. But the \"numbered markers on content that is not a sequence\" — method IS a sequence, so OK.\n\nLet me write ResearchLive. I'll define the method steps and the fixed-by table data as module attrs.\n\nThen AboutLive: who JobyCorp is and why the work is shared. Keep it prose + at least one fi (truncated)
