INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 73, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nThe self-import breaks compilation. Let me revert the app-wide import and import per-LiveView instead.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "      # JobyKit-shipped wrappers: <.button>, <.card>, <.icon>, <.input>,\n      # <.flash>, <.flash_group>, <.header>, <.list>, <.table>.\n      import JobyKit.CoreComponents", "old_string" => "      # JobyKit-shipped wrappers: <.button>, <.card>, <.icon>, <.input>,\n      # <.flash>, <.flash_group>, <.header>, <.list>, <.table>.\n      import JobyKit.CoreComponents\n\n      # This app's registered composites: <.record_card>, <.spec_row>.\n      import BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents", "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/lib/benchapp_web.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-bf53411a5d884b9a", "name" => "edit"}], "Right, the self-import problem. Since `CompositeComponents` does `use BenchappWeb, :html`, and now html_helpers imports `BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents`, it tries to import itself → error.\n\nOptions:\n1. Don't import CompositeComponents app-wide. Instead alias it and call `<CompositeComponents.record_card ...>` in the LiveViews.\n2. Keep app-wide import but make composite_components.ex not `use BenchappWeb, :html` (use `use Phoenix.Component` directly + import needed helpers). But it needs `~H`, which comes from Phoenix.Component. And it doesn't use CoreComponents now. So I can `use Phoenix.Component`. But then verified_routes (~p) not available — record_card/spec_row don't use ~p. And Gettext not needed. That works but deviates from pattern.\n\nOption 1 is cleaner and matches kit style (layouts use full module names). But then HomeLive etc need `alias BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents` and call `<CompositeComponents.record_card>`. That's more verbose but fine.\n\nActually, a nicer option: keep the app-wide import for call sites, but guard the self-import by making CompositeComponents `use BenchappWeb, :html` work. The conflict is the import of itself. I could remove `import BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents` from html_helpers and instead have the LiveViews do their own `import BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents`. Then composite_components.ex uses `use BenchappWeb, :html` which does NOT import itself → no conflict. And each LiveView imports it locally. That keeps `<.record_card>` shorthand and avoids self-import.\n\nWait but design_previews.ex also `use BenchappWeb, :html` and calls `CompositeComponents.record_card` (aliased) — fine. And design_manifest aliases. Fine.\n\nBut LiveViews importing `BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents` — do the LiveViews define that module? No. So no self-import conflict. Good.\n\nSo plan: revert html_helpers change (remove the app-wide import), and add `import BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents` in each LiveView? Actually simpler: revert html_helpers, and in each LiveView (Home, Research, About) the `use BenchappWeb, :live_view` triggers html_helpers. If I don't want to edit every LiveView, app-wide import is nicer. But app-wide import breaks CompositeComponents itself.\n\nCleanest: use a dedicated helper. Let me instead NOT import in html_helpers. Instead I'll keep the composites aliased and call with namespace in LiveViews. That avoids editing html_helpers and avoids per-view imports. Let me revert the html_helpers edit.\n\nActually the brief says \"Compose the kit's registered wrappers\" and shorthand `<.name>` is nicer but namespaced form is fully acceptable (kit itself uses `JobyKit.NavComponent.simple_nav`, `JobyKit.CoreComponents.theme_toggle`, `JobyKit.PageComponent.custom_page_component`). So namespaced is fine.\n\nBut I'd prefer `<.record_card>` shorthand for readability. Let me revert the app-wide import and just add `import BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents` to each LiveView module individually (Home/Research/About). Since those modules aren't CompositeComponents, no self-import. That gives shorthand and avoids conflict.\n\nLet me revert html_helpers.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:44:58.905431Z], "9b02e0a0-1fea-435a-94f4-0ccab83b55da"]
