INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 87, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nLint flags duplicated page-level class strings across my three pages. The intended fix is to lift these repeated patterns into registered composites. Let me check whether previews are required in the manifest first.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/deps/joby_kit/lib/joby_kit/manifest.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-bed860b4b2b28e28", "name" => "read"}], "The lint flags `duplicated_class_string` warnings. These are the repeated Tailwind utility class strings used across the three pages for section headings, table borders, running heads, etc. The lint considers ≥3 uses of the same ≥25-char class string a signal to lift into a wrapper.\n\nThese warnings matter because... does `mix joby_kit.lint` FAIL (non-zero exit) on warnings, or only on errors? The summary says \"10 warnings.\" Let me check the Mix task exit code. Warnings likely don't fail the task unless configured with --warnings-as-errors. The brief says \"Lint must be clean.\" So I should eliminate warnings too.\n\nThese duplicated strings come from my repeated page-level patterns:\n- `class=\"max-w-prose space-y-3\"` (28-char) ×3 → section intro wrapper\n- `class=\"text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl\"` (49-char) ×6 → section h2 heading\n- `class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg\"` (69? actually 57) ×7 → section lead paragraph\n- `class=\"overflow-x-auto rounded-box border border-base-300\"` (50) ×3 → table container\n- `class=\"[&>thead>tr>th]:bg-base-200\"` (25) ×5 → table header class\n- `class=\"flex items-baseline gap-3\"` (30) ×3 → running head wrapper\n- `class=\"space-y-8 border-t border-base-300 py-16 md:py-24\"` (49? 57) → section container\n- `class=\"font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70\"` (38) ×6 → mono running-head text\n- `class=\"font-mono text-sm\"` (25? actually short) \n\nSo I have multiple repeated \"semantic UI object\" patterns. Per the kit's own guidance: \"the same semantic UI object appears with the same classes on more than one page → lift it into a component.\" These ARE page-level patterns I reuse. I should lift them into composites/wrappers. That's exactly what the brief's \"composite used on more than one page\" wants, and it's the clean fix.\n\nLet me design more composites to absorb these repeated patterns, which also improves consistency:\n\n1. `section_heading` — the h2 with `text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl`. But it's a heading (h2), a primitive? Not a raw HTML primitive but it IS repeated. Lint flags it. Lift into a component `section_head` that renders the running head + heading + lead paragraph as one \"data section opener\"? DESIGN describes: \"A section that presents data may open with a hairline and a short monospace running head... Prose sections open with their heading and nothing else.\"\n\nLet me create a `data_section` / `prose_section` pattern. But to be careful and general, let me make focused composites:\n\nA) `section_intro` (running head + h2 + lead) — composes the running-head span, h2, and lead paragraph. This absorbs several duplicated strings: the running head wrapper `flex items-baseline gap-3`, the mono label `font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70`, the h2 classes, the lead paragraph classes, and the `max-w-prose space-y-3` wrapper.\n\nB) `figure_table` or just wrap the table container? The table container `overflow-x-auto rounded-box border border-base-300` repeated 3× and `[&>thead>tr>th]:bg-base-200` 5×. I could lift the table into a composite `data_table` that wraps `<.table>` with the container + header styling. That removes both those duplicated strings. \n\nC) The section container `space-y-8 border-t border-base-300 py-16 md:py-24` and `max-w-prose space-y-4` (spec sheets) and `max-w-prose space-y-3` etc. And the lead paragraph `text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg` repeated a lot.\n\nThis is getting into many composites. Let me think about the cleanest set that eliminates ≥3 duplicates. The threshold is 3 occurrences (≥3). If a string appears only 2×, it's fine. So I need to bring every ≥25-char class string down to ≤2 occurrences OR vary them.\n\nStrategy: Build composites that encapsulate the repeated visual patterns, so the class strings live once inside the composite and call sites use `<.section_intro>`, `<.data_table>`, `<.lead>`, etc. That's the intended fix and improves the design system.\n\nLet me define these composites in CompositeComponents:\n\n1. `data_section` — a bordered section container with an optional running head +" <> ..., ~U[2026-09-11 08:49:59.003422Z], "8f43dfcd-3c8d-49c3-a543-ec554c7a2d4c"]
