INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 89, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nThe clean fix is to lift the repeated page patterns into registered composites. Let me rewrite `composite_components.ex` with a small set of page-chrome composites.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"content" => "defmodule BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Generic, multi-primitive composites for this app.\n\n  Composites live one layer above core wrappers: they bundle a small set\n  of `JobyKit.CoreComponents` primitives and theme tokens into a\n  higher-level pattern that appears more than once across the site.\n\n  Every composite follows the JobyKit wrapper contract:\n\n    1. Declare every prop with `attr` (use `values:` for variant enums).\n    2. Carry `data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.<name>\"`\n       on the root element.\n    3. Accept `attr :rest, :global` for id/class/aria-*/phx-* pass-through.\n    4. Internals compose theme tokens and the plotting-paper surface —\n       never raw `<button>`/`<input>`/`<textarea>`.\n    5. Register the composite in `BenchappWeb.DesignManifest`\n       (`category: :composite`) so it surfaces on `/custom-designs` and\n       in `/design.json`.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use BenchappWeb, :html\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  A JobyCorp run record shown as a specimen: the fields a record carries\n  and the unit each quantity is reported in, set in monospace on a\n  plotting-paper surface framed by the accent trace. Field names and\n  units only — never invented values. An optional caption sits under the\n  card in the secondary text colour.\n\n      <.record_card\n        title=\"run record\"\n        fields={[%{field: \"ttft\", unit: \"ms\"}]}\n        caption=\"What every published run carries.\"\n      />\n  \"\"\"\n  attr :fields, :list, required: true, doc: \"List of `%{field:, unit:}` maps.\"\n  attr :title, :string, default: \"run record\"\n  attr :caption, :string, default: nil, doc: \"One-line caption beneath the card.\"\n  attr :class, :any, default: nil\n  attr :rest, :global\n\n  def record_card(assigns) do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <div data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.record_card\" class={@class} {@rest}>\n      <div class=\"plotting-paper rounded-box p-6\">\n        <div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-secondary/40 pb-2\">\n          <span class=\"font-mono text-sm text-base-content\">{@title}</span>\n          <span class=\"font-mono text-[0.7rem] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-base-content/70\">\n            record\n          </span>\n        </div>\n        <dl class=\"pt-1 font-mono text-sm\">\n          <div\n            :for={f <- @fields}\n            class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-b border-secondary/20 py-1.5 last:border-0\"\n          >\n            <dt class=\"text-base-content\">{f.field}</dt>\n            <dd class=\"text-base-content/70\">{f.unit}</dd>\n          </div>\n        </dl>\n      </div>\n      <p :if={@caption} class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-base-content/70\">\n        {@caption}\n      </p>\n    </div>\n    \"\"\"\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  A spec-sheet row: a monospace label in a fixed column beside a reading\n  column. From `md` the two sit side by side; at phone width they stack.\n  Use several in a `space-y-*` container to build a spec sheet.\n\n      <.spec_row label=\"method\">Each model is run locally, on hardware we own.</.spec_row>\n  \"\"\"\n  attr :label, :string, required: true, doc: \"Monospace label in the fixed column.\"\n  attr :class, :any, default: nil\n  attr :rest, :global\n  slot :inner_block, required: true, doc: \"Reading column content.\"\n\n  def spec_row(assigns) do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <div\n      data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.spec_row\"\n      class={[\"border-t border-base-300 pt-4 md:flex md:gap-8\", @class]}\n      {@rest}\n    >\n      <dt class=\"w-44 shrink-0 pb-1 font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70 md:pb-0\">\n        {@label}\n      </dt>\n      <dd class=\"text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed\">{render_slot(@inner_block)}</dd>\n    </div>\n    \"\"\"\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  The centred page column: `max-w-6xl`, `px-6` at phone width, `px-8`\n  from `md`. One per page; sections live inside it.\n  \"\"\"\n  attr :class, :any, default: nil\n  attr :rest, :global\n  slot :inner_block, required: true\n\n  def page_body(assigns) do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <div\n      data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.page_body\"\n      class={[\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-8\", @class]}\n      {@rest}\n    >\n      {render_s" <> ..., "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/lib/benchapp_web/components/composite_components.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-8470de04d3ba132b", "name" => "write"}], "Preview is optional. But my composites are registered. I want the duplicate-class lint clean. The right move: lift the repeated page-level patterns into registered composites. Let me identify the recurring patterns:\n\n1. The `border-t border-base-300 py-16 md:py-24` + inner `space-y-8` section wrapper — appears many times. → make a `Section` composite with an optional running-head (mono `measure`/`method`) and title + lead paragraph.\n2. The table container: `overflow-x-auto rounded-box border border-base-300` + `[&>thead>tr>th]:bg-base-200` on the `.table`. → make a `figure_table` composite that wraps `.table`.\n3. The running-head line `flex items-baseline gap-3` with mono label.\n4. The hero grid wrapper.\n5. The h2 `text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl`.\n6. The `max-w-prose space-y-3` heading group.\n\nLet me design a set of registered composites that these pages compose:\n\n- `section/1` — a content section with hairline + optional `head` (mono running head), `title`, optional lead paragraph, and inner content. props: head, title, lead (slot), rest.\n- `data_section/1` — same as section (head + title + lead) but for data sections.\n\nLet me look again at the patterns I want to remove.\n\nRepeated class strings:\n- `\"flex items-baseline gap-3\"` — running head wrapper (5×)\n- `\"font-mono text-sm text-base-content/70\"` — the mono running-head label (6×)\n- `\"max-w-prose space-y-3\"` (3×)\n- `\"text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl\"` — section h2 (5×)\n- `\"text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg\"` (6×) — lead paragraph\n- `\"space-y-8 border-t border-base-300 py-16 md:py-24\"` (3×+) — section wrapper\n- `\"max-w-prose space-y-4\"` — spec sheet container (3×)\n- `\"text-sm text-base-content/80\"` — table cell copy (4×)\n- `\"overflow-x-auto rounded-box border border-base-300\"` (3×)\n- `\"[&>thead>tr>th]:bg-base-200\"` (3×)\n- `\"font-mono text-sm\"` — table mono cell (used inside tables, several)\n- `\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-8\"` (3×)\n\nI should design composites for these. The cleanest approach: build a `PageComponents`/composites that encapsulate the section chrome and table figure. Let me create these composites:\n\n1. `page_body/1` — `<div class=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-8\">` wrapper, slot inner_block. (removes page container dup)\n2. `section/1` — data/section block with hairline, running head, title, lead, content:\n   - attr `head` (mono label, optional — omitted for prose sections)\n   - attr `title`, required\n   - slot `lead`\n   - slot inner_block (content)\n   - root: `<section class=\"space-y-8 border-t border-base-300 py-16 md:py-24\">` and inner heading group `max-w-prose space-y-3`, running-head line, h2 with the type scale, lead `<p class=\"text-base leading-relaxed text-base-content/70 md:text-lg\">`.\n3. `figure_table/1` — wraps `<.table>` in `overflow-x-auto rounded-box border border-base-300` and sets `zebra=false` + `[&>thead>tr>th]:bg-base-200`. But it needs to forward cols slots. Forwarding `. (truncated)
