INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 111, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nLint is clean. Now let me write render tests for each page.\n\n\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"content" => "defmodule BenchappWeb.HomeLiveTest do\n  use BenchappWeb.ConnCase, async: true\n\n  import Phoenix.LiveViewTest\n\n  test \"renders the landing page chrome and content\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, ~p\"/\")\n\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#main-nav\")\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#theme-toggle\")\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#nav-toggle\")\n    assert has_element?(view, \"h1\")\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{[data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.record_card\"]})\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{a[href=\"/research\"]})\n  end\n\n  test \"marks the current page in the nav\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, ~p\"/\")\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{#main-nav a[aria-current=\"page\"][href=\"/\"]})\n  end\n\n  test \"does not link to the kit inspection routes\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, _view, html} = live(conn, ~p\"/\")\n    refute html =~ ~s{href=\"/design\"}\n    refute html =~ \"/custom-designs\"\n    refute html =~ \"/design.json\"\n  end\nend\n", "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/home_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-9eac83a21118ca10", "name" => "write"}, %{"arguments" => %{"content" => "defmodule BenchappWeb.ResearchLiveTest do\n  use BenchappWeb.ConnCase, async: true\n\n  import Phoenix.LiveViewTest\n\n  test \"renders the research page\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, ~p\"/research\")\n\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#main-nav\")\n    assert has_element?(view, \"h1\")\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{[data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.record_card\"]})\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{[data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.figure_table\"]})\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#fixed\")\n  end\n\n  test \"marks the current page in the nav\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, ~p\"/research\")\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{#main-nav a[aria-current=\"page\"][href=\"/research\"]})\n  end\nend\n", "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/research_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-aaf12623a0743f97", "name" => "write"}, %{"arguments" => %{"content" => "defmodule BenchappWeb.AboutLiveTest do\n  use BenchappWeb.ConnCase, async: true\n\n  import Phoenix.LiveViewTest\n\n  test \"renders the about page\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, ~p\"/about\")\n\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#main-nav\")\n    assert has_element?(view, \"h1\")\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{[data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.figure_table\"]})\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#shared\")\n  end\n\n  test \"marks the current page in the nav\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, ~p\"/about\")\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{#main-nav a[aria-current=\"page\"][href=\"/about\"]})\n  end\nend\n", "path" => "/Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/about_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-98904ebd321dca64", "name" => "write"}], "Lint clean. Now let me write render tests for each page. Let me look at the existing test files to model the new tests, and understand ConnCase usage for LiveView testing.\n\nI'll create test/benchapp_web/live/home_live_test.exs, research_live_test.exs, about_live_test.exs. Use `use BenchappWeb.ConnCase, async: true`. Since these LiveViews don't use Repo, but ConnCase sets up sandbox — fine. Use `live(conn, ~p\"/\")` and assert on element IDs.\n\nLet me write tests asserting:\n- Home: has #main-nav, has #theme-toggle, page content e.g. the hero h1 or the record_card data-component, a link to /research. Also verify no links to /design, /custom-designs, /design.json.\n- Research: has record_card (data-component), #measures? no, #fixed table tbody id. has nav.\n- About: #shared table, nav.\n- Also test aria-current on nav for each page.\n- Also test nav-toggle and mobile menu exist.\n\nLet me also add a test that removed demo content is gone (no \"built with\", no /design link). And the composite preview host — /custom-designs still works (route in place). I could add a test but not required.\n\nLet me be careful: `live_isolated`? No, use `live(conn, path)` with full layout. The nav ids (#main-nav, #theme-toggle, #nav-toggle) come from Layouts.app which is rendered. Good.\n\nFor aria-current check: `has_element?(view, ~s{a[aria-current=\"page\"][href=\"/research\"]})`. The `.link navigate` renders `<a href=\"/research\" data-phx-link=\"redirect\"?...>`. Actually `<.link navigate={~p\"/research\"}>` renders `<a data-phx-link=\"patch|redirect\"... href=\"/research\">`? navigate renders `href=\"/research\"`. It should have the href attribute. And aria-current set only for active. Let me assert on the active page: for home `a[aria-current=\"page\"][href=\"/\"]`.\n\nLet me verify how `.link navigate` renders aria-current. `.link` passes aria-current via rest to `<a>`. Should render `aria-current=\"page\"`. Good.\n\nLet me write the tests. Use element/2, has_element?/2.\n\nLet me model after typical Phoenix LV tests:\n```\ndefmodule BenchappWeb.HomeLiveTest do\n  use BenchappWeb.ConnCase, async: true\n  import Phoenix.LiveViewTest\n\n  test \"renders landing content\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, ~p\"/\")\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#main-nav\")\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#theme-toggle\")\n    assert has_element?(view, \"#nav-toggle\")\n    assert has_element?(view, \"h1\")\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{[data-component=\"BenchappWeb.CompositeComponents.record_card\"]})\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{a[href=\"/research\"]})\n  end\n\n  test \"marks the current page\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _} = live(conn, ~p\"/\")\n    assert has_element?(view, ~s{#main-nav a[aria-current=\"page\"][href=\"/\"]})\n  end\n\n  test \"no links to kit inspection routes\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, _view, html} = live(conn, ~p\"/\")\n    refute html =~ \"/design\"\n    refute html =~ \"/custom-designs\"\n    refute html =~ \"/design.json\"\n  end\nend\n```\nWait `refute html =~ \"/design\"` — \"/design.json\" contains \"/design\". And also the theme-toggle etc don't contain /design. But careful: the home page has NO /design links now. But `~p\"/\"` links: footer + nav link href=\"/research\" etc. Does any rendered attr contain \"/design\"? The root layout includes `/assets/css/app.css` (not \"/design\"). Good. But wait — `refute html =~ \"/design\"` would also catch \"/design.json\" and \"/custom-designs\"? \"/custom-designs\" contains substring \"design\" but not \"/design\"? \"/custom-designs\" → contains \"/design\"? c-u-s-t-o-m-...-designs → \"-designs\" not \"/design\". No \"/design\" substring. Good. But to be safe I'll check each explicitly with `refute html =~ ~s{href=\"/design\"}` etc. Simpler: check `refute html =~ ~s{href=\"/design\"}` and `refute html =~ \"/custom-designs\"` and `refute html =~ \"/design.json\"`. That's robust.\n\nActually the requirement is \"nothing on the site may link to or mention them.\" My site pages don't. Good. But the /custom-designs and /design pages themselves exist and mention each other — but those aren't linked. The test only checks my three pages.\n\nNow the nav-toggle uses JS.toggle; the mobile menu starts `" <> ..., ~U[2026-09-11 08:57:14.195272Z], "69319b42-e494-4e73-9951-6a97c4c452e7"]
