INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 132, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nHome renders beautifully in dark. Let me verify the light theme via the toggle.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"action" => "click", "selector" => "#theme-toggle button[aria-label=\"Light theme\"]"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-8df857ec0bb58125", "name" => "preview"}], "The page opened in dark theme (the browser's stored preference is dark or the default). It looks great — the record card with plotting-paper grid in teal, monospace, hero headline tight. Nav shows Home highlighted teal. This is dark theme actually. Scheme said light but the theme toggle default was \"system\" → the browser prefers dark, so it's showing dark theme. The theme is fine. \n\nThe design looks strong and on-brief. Let me verify the light theme too. But note the scheme label says \"light\" yet rendered dark — because the root layout script sets data-theme from localStorage/system, overriding the emulated scheme. That's the app's own theme system working. The theme toggle (system/light/dark) controls it. Good — both themes need checking. Let me explicitly set dark and light via the toggle buttons to confirm both are finished.\n\nActually the emulated `scheme` (CDP prefers-color-scheme) isn't respected because the app persists choice via localStorage and defaults to system only when no stored value. The screenshot is dark. Let me test the toggle to see light. I'll click the light theme toggle (hero-sun button, second in the join) and screenshot.\n\nLet me be efficient. I'll click light toggle on home and screenshot top.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:58:11.885176Z], "ead87ea1-df04-4f9f-bc9e-4df5e32f7bb9"]
