 Let me change to just \"method\" (the section is \"Local by construction\" about method/hardware). Actually \"hardware\" fits \"what is measured\" better. The section is about hardware+method. I'll use \"method\". Hmm but I have another research section with head \"method\". To keep them distinct, this home section could be head=\"hardware\". Let me use \"hardware\". Actually the section is about local hardware AND method. I'll title the running head \"method\" — no, research already uses method. Two different pages can both say method but better distinct. Let me set home hardware/method section head to \"hardware\". That names what is measured/held. Fine. Remove the middle dot.\n\nAlso reconsider: are there other middle dots in meta strings? Footer sentence only. Good.\n\nLet me fix the home section head from \"hardware · method\" to \"hardware\".\n\nAlso the spec rows render well (mono label column + reading column with hairline between). Good.\n\nNow the \"Local by construction\" spec rows have a top hairline via border-t on spec_row — looks good.\n\nLet me change the head. Then continue reviewing phone widths and research/about pages.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:58:56.097090Z], "d2cffbc1-73b2-4361-9d6b-76577a89e341"]
