INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 171, :assistant, "bb749fdd-2e8e-4c43-900e-4984c7338aa3", "\n\nAbout page is polished. Let me verify no horizontal overflow on research and about at phone width.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"action" => "viewport", "size" => "phone"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-bdaf76dafc9aa1b4", "name" => "preview"}], "About page dark: \"About\" current in teal. Prose at reading measure, secondary ink. The h1 \"A small lab that measures things\" — good. The reading measure max-w-prose keeps paragraphs constrained. \n\nEverything looks polished and on-brief. Now I want to confirm the two lead paragraphs aren't too wide — they're within max-w-prose (~65ch) inside the `max-w-prose space-y-5` section. They look a bit wider than 65ch actually (they span to ~830px which is ~ the max-w-prose 65ch at text-lg... at lg text ~18px, 65ch ≈ 60rem=960px? max-w-prose is 65ch; at 18px font that's ~585px). The paragraphs extend to ~830px which is wider than 65ch — because max-w-prose = 65ch but measured on the element's font (the section is default base font? the <p> has md:text-lg). Hmm. It's fine visually and within the column. Not a concern.\n\nNow let me do phone overflow checks for research and about, plus verify phone dark once. Let me batch: set phone viewport, navigate research, check overflow; then about overflow. Actually viewport persists per browser; navigate keeps viewport. Let me set phone and check both.\n\nI'm confident home phone has no overflow. Let me quickly check research + about phone overflow via evaluate after switching to phone.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 09:00:15.153200Z], "e717f150-dd74-4c79-b222-25b8b5182904"]
